A||N||1||soup||87 GT Fiero w/ T-Tops questions.||||1||
Z||000000||soup||11-09-2001||07:45 PM||||I own an 87 fiero GT with T-Tops. I read somewhere on the net that in all the years they made the Fiero there were only 1000 of them that came from the factory with T-Tops. I was wondering if this is true and if this is why my fiero has "special edition" stickers on it. Also I was wondering how much my car would be worth to a collector if this is true if it was in excelent original condition. Basically any information about my car would be helpfull. Thanks, you can email me at soup@soupk.com or just post here.||||reg||1
Z||000001||T-top Fiero||11-09-2001||08:50 PM||||Only the 88's could be ordered with "factory" T-tops (code CJB on the options sticker), but the conversion was done by aftermarket company C&C. All other year T-tops were done through C&C dealers in the aftermarket.<BR>As to why your car has "special edition" stickers on it, maybe a previous owner added them.<P>Pat||||reg||1
